{
  "about": "FABRIC-GRAPH1's review, finding 1 (FIX-LOG 2026-10-17): a writer of driver.json keeps every key it does not own, in its place, and an edit changes only what it edits. Read row for row by the CLI's configkeeps.test.ts and the driver's DriverConfigKeepsTests. `file` is an existing file in the writer's layout, its lines joined by LF with one final LF: every key Setup and the terminal write, and keys neither twin knows at the top, in a landing rule and in a workspace rule, a cycle with numbers JavaScript cannot hold, a cycle that is not an object, a kind of work no unit reads and an empty map. A row's `edit` is one door's change (`op` and its fields); `changes` turn `file` into what both twins write, each `from` found exactly once (its lines joined by LF) and replaced by `to`. The re-check (finding 1, 3): a row's `between` is another writer's change, made to the file after this writer read it and before it writes, which the write keeps; a row whose file `crlf` is true has its lines joined by CRLF, and so is what both write; a row `refused` writes nothing, its refusal naming what it says (empty: any refusal), the file left as `between` made it. `twice` is one rule for a key written twice in one object: read as its last value in its first place (JavaScript's own reading), and never edited. The second re-check: an edit is the set of key paths it changed, and touches those alone on the file as it stands, so an object another writer took out is made again with only the edit's own keys under it, never its old ones, and one another writer made a string or an array refuses the edit, naming the path; a row `missing` is read where no file was, and another writer's file made before the write is kept, or refused, as any other. CONFIG1 (D173's note): `sets` names the arrays that are sets, which both twins carry (`DriverConfig.Sets`, `DRIVER_SETS`), each a key path with `*` any one name; an edit of one is the names it added and took, compared without case, made onto the file's array as it stands, so two writers adding to one set keep both (the CONFIGMERGE1 rows). `names` holds each per-name map both twins read (`map`), a `file` writing a name twice in any case, and the map `read` from it, its entries in order: a name is read where first readable, its first spelling and value (CASEMAP1). `lock` holds the stale rules of the lock a keeping write holds from its re-read to its rename (CONFIGLOCK1, `KeepLock`, `keeplock.ts`): a row's `pid` (`live` or `gone`, as the test's liveness answers) and `age` in seconds make the lock's text `{ pid, since }`, or `text` is the lock's text whole; `stale` is what both twins judge.",
